The effect replicates on Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct: extreme-BCS gaps of $-$27.1\,pp (count 8) and $-$23.9\,pp (count 16), reaching 77--87\% of Qwen3-32B's gap (Table~\ref{tab:cross_model_bcs}). All three scales (Qwen3-32B, Llama-70B, Llama-8B) show consistent negative BCS slopes on FewRel RE (Appendix~\ref{sec:appendix_cross_model_70b}). Gemini~2.5~Flash provides partial but fragile corroboration ($\Delta = -17.6$\,pp at count 8; Appendix~\ref{sec:appendix_cross_model_gemini}). Llama-8B and Llama-70B both show no NER BCS signal ($r{=}{-}0.13$, $p{=}0.36$ for 70B), confirming the task asymmetry across three models (Table~\ref{tab:cross_model_ner_null}).

