\paragraph{Prompt sensitivity.}
\looseness=-1
Under the v2 prompt, the extreme-batch BCS gap is $-$25.5\,pp ($r = -0.919$, $p < 0.001$; $n{=}25$), modestly attenuated from v1 but highly significant. NER shows no batch-level BCS--F1 correlation under either prompt ($r \approx 0$, $n = 450$; \S\ref{sec:multi_channel}). The effect holds across four structurally distinct prompt variants at count 32 (all $r \leq -0.47$; Appendix~\ref{sec:appendix_prompt_variants}), ruling out prompt design as the source. Few-shot demonstrations widen the confusability gap (+4.3\,pp under 5-shot), though this finding is limited to a single dataset (Appendix~\ref{sec:appendix_fewshot_bcs}).

